If there is a patient then every clinician should reassess a pain for the patient and should reassess a function for the patient and should reassess a treatment-course for the patient.
If a patient has a chronic-pain and a potentially-reversible-cause causes the chronic-pain then every clinician should address the potentially-reversible-cause.
If a pain-management-optimization is needed for a patient then every clinician should optimize a pain-management for the patient.
